 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Audit Workflow Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an audit workflow?\", \"a\": \"An audit workflow is the ordered set of steps an audit follows, with a person and a deadline attached to each one. A typical audit has four stages: planning, fieldwork, reporting, and follow-up. The workflow is the work inside those stages: each request answered and each finding closed.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to design efficient audit workflow processes?\", \"a\": \"Design it around the items that move, not the calendar. Give every item one owner, one due date, and one place for its evidence. Then set the day each reminder goes out and the day a late item escalates. Reuse last year's list as the starting point. In Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder'>AI automation builder</a>, you write those rules in plain English and get a working app.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to automate audit workflow and task assignments?\", \"a\": \"Assign by rule instead of by email. Map each request type or control to a role, such as bank reconciliations to the AP lead, and have the app create every task with its due date when the audit opens. When someone changes jobs, you update one mapping. Emergent builds that assignment logic from a plain-English prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to automate compliance and audit workflows?\", \"a\": \"Automate the controls first, then the audit of them. When approvals and reconciliations already run in software, each one leaves a dated record, and the audit becomes pulling records instead of chasing emails. <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/purchase-order-automation'>Purchase order automation</a> is one place to start: each order's approver and amount are logged when the order is placed.\"}, {\"q\": \"How digital platforms simplify audit workflows?\", \"a\": \"They replace the shared spreadsheet and the email chain with one record per item that holds its owner and its files. Reminders go out on schedule, and the auditor sees what is late without a status call. When you compare audit workflow tools, check that the record carries over into next year's audit.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to automate data extraction in audit workflows?\", \"a\": \"Use an AI step that reads each document into fields, starting with documents that arrive in volume and share a layout, such as bank statements and vendor invoices. Match those fields against the ledger and show the tester only the differences. Apps built with Emergent can include that reading step and pull the ledger side through an API.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you implement a paperless audit workflow?\", \"a\": \"Pick one place for every file, then stop accepting evidence by email or on paper. Scan paper records once, at the source, and name each scan by its request number. Record approvals as a dated click in the app instead of initials on a printout. For letters your team sends, such as bank confirmation requests, <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/document-automation'>document automation</a> can fill them from a template.\"}, {\"q\": \"How can a team improve audit workflow collaboration?\", \"a\": \"Work from one shared list instead of separate trackers. Let auditors and request owners see the same status for each item, and keep questions as comments on the item itself, where the next person can read them, not in email threads. Hold one short weekly review of late items only, and name who acts on each one before the call ends.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to use ai to speed up audit workflows?\", \"a\": \"Use AI where the work is reading and writing, and keep the judgment with the auditor. Three tasks suit it: drafting a finding from the tester's notes, summarizing a long management response, and comparing this year's findings with last year's to spot repeats. Have a person review each draft before it goes into the report.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should I look for in audit workflow software?\", \"a\": \"Look first at who you pay for. Request owners outside finance may answer two items a year, and per-user pricing charges for each of them. Then confirm you can export every file and decision when the audit ends. Emergent builds the app on a database you own, with full code export on paid plans.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
